commit 157c5f42a41d808d951d335136a82dd57433871a
Author:     Yixun-Hu <yixunhu21@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Thu Sep 3 16:21:24 2026 -0400
Commit:     Yixun-Hu <yixunhu21@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Thu Sep 3 16:21:24 2026 -0400

    ViT gradient checkpointing for the geometry conditioner
    
    The C4 frame average runs the DINOv3 backbone once per orbit angle, so the
    ViT sees |orbit| x micro-batch activations per step -- too much for a 48GB
    card at micro-batch 32. Opt-in activation checkpointing on the encoder layers
    collapses that peak with numerically identical weights and gradients.
    
    - _make_vit_ckpt_forward: instance-level wrapper; checkpoints only in
      training mode with grad enabled (eval/no_grad passes are zero-overhead);
      use_reentrant=False for DDP find-unused compatibility; the checkpoint
      function is resolved by attribute at call time so tests can observe it
    - _checkpoint_vit_layers: wraps every encoder layer (.layer nn.ModuleList),
      idempotent across the two conditioners sharing one backbone, fail-closed
      ValueError on backbones without a usable layer list; registers nothing, so
      the state_dict is byte-identical. Deliberately does not rely on HF's
      gradient_checkpointing_enable() -- in transformers 4.57.0 that path binds
      the checkpoint function opaquely in a base-class hook and gates only on
      .training, invisible to instrumentation
    - GeometryConditioner(gradient_checkpointing=False): absent/off is
      byte-identical behaviour; the config key flows through the factory as-is
    - tests (stub backbones, no download): wrap-once + atol=0 value identity,
      no-checkpoint under eval AND under no_grad (separate tests -- the no_grad
      gate needs its own), shared-backbone idempotency, state-dict ON/OFF
      identity, fail-closed family, absent-flag no-op; the DINOv3-backed
      integration tests land in the companion commit
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012ztmGNBHC4RogGPd9gYHJA

