   331	      the ``[0, 90]`` a sibling config declares, and a non-numeric string would
   332	      surface as a bare ``ValueError`` from deep inside a comprehension;
   333	    * ``NaN`` / ``inf`` -- ``NaN != NaN``, so an orbit containing one can never
   334	      compare equal to itself and a protocol guard built on orbit comparison
   335	      would report a mismatch against the very checkpoint the orbit came from;
   336	    * a non-sequence (a ``dict``, a bare string, a scalar) -- iterated blindly it
   337	      turns into per-key or per-character "angles" instead of failing.
