   100	## Training 
   101	
   102	### FLAC
   103	To start a training run on the AcousticRooms dataset, run the `train.py` script in the repo root with:
   104	```bash
   105	python train.py \
   106	--dataset-config src/configs/dataset_configs/AR/train/acousticroom_train.json \
   107	--val-dataset-config src/configs/dataset_configs/AR/eval/acousticroom_seeneval.json \
   108	--val-every 2500 \
   109	--checkpoint-every 2500 \
   110	--batch-size 64 \
   111	--num-workers 8 \
   112	--model-config src/configs/model_configs/FLAC/AR/FLAC_AR.json \
   113	--pretransform-ckpt-path weights/FLAC/VAE.safetensors \
   114	--save-dir ./outputs_FLAC \
   115	--experiment-name FLAC_training \
   116	--name FLAC
   117	```
   118	
   119	### VAE
   120	The VAE takes multiple days on an H100. We provide a pretrained checkpoint (3.08M steps). To train from scratch:
   121	```bash
   122	python train.py \
   123	--dataset-config src/configs/dataset_configs/AR/train/acousticroom_train.json \
   124	--val-dataset-config src/configs/dataset_configs/AR/eval/acousticroom_seeneval.json \
   125	--model-config src/configs/model_configs/VAE/VAE.json \
   126	--batch-size 64 \
   127	--num-workers 8 \
   128	--val-every 10000 \
   129	--save-dir ./outputs_VAE \
   130	--name VAE \
   131	--experiment-name VAE_training
   132	```
   133	**Note**: Trained VAE checkpoints must be processed via `unwrap_model.py` before use in FLAC training.
   134	
   135	### Finetuning on HAA
   136	To finetune FLAC pretrained on AR on the HAA dataset, run:
   137	```bash
   138	python train.py \
   139	--dataset-config src/configs/dataset_configs/HAA/train/haa_train.json \
   140	--val-dataset-config src/configs/dataset_configs/HAA/eval/haa_val.json \
   141	--model-config src/configs/model_configs/FLAC/HAA/FLAC_HAA_finetune.json \
   142	--val-every 10 \
   143	--checkpoint-every 10 \
   144	--max-steps 1000 \
   145	--num-workers 8 \
   146	--batch-size 16 \
   147	--accum-batches 4 \
   148	--name FLAC_HAA \
   149	--pretransform-ckpt-path weights/FLAC/VAE.safetensors \
   150	--pretrained-ckpt-path weights/FLAC/FLAC_EMA.ckpt
   151	```
   152	Because the dataset is small, we accumulate gradients over 4 batches to increase the effective batch size.
   153	
   154	**Performance Tip**: Removing the minus in `src/configs/dataset_configs/custom_metadata/HAA_md.py` (L70) improves acoustic metrics for HAA. This is consistent with the fact that the setup is reversed compared to AR (depth at the source position instead of the listener position). See the paper supplementary material for more details on this.
   155	
   156	**Paper Metrics**: To obtain the metrics presented in the paper, we averaged over individual results per scene. The evaluation script also provides a mean over all the samples from all the scenes, which is different.
   157	
   158	### FLAC Config Variants
   159	We provide the config for different models from our paper. 
   160	| Config File | Conditioning | Description |
   161	| ----------- | ------------ | ----------- |
   162	| `FLAC_AR.json` | AdaLN + Cross-Attn | Baseline. |
   163	| `FLAC_AR_S.json` | AdaLN + Cross-Attn | Smaller DiT (Depth of 4). Similar performances. |
   164	| `FLAC_AR_FA.json` | AdaLN + Cross-Attn | Frame-averaged (yaw-equivariant) conditioning; see the dedicated section below. |
   165	| `FLAC_AR_AllCA.json` | Cross-Attn| All conditioning via cross-attention. |
   166	| `FLAC_AR_InContext.json` | Prepended | Conditioning prepended to input sequence. |
   167	| `FLAC_AR_VAECtxt.json` | AdaLN + Cross-Attn | Uses VAE to encode context RIRs instead of ResNet18. Works with dataset config `acousticroom_train_VAECtxt.json`|
   168	| `FLAC_AR_noGeom.json` | AdaLN + Cross-Attn | Evaluates FLAC without geometric conditioning (ablation).|
