   289	
   290	### Baselines
   291	We provide a unified evaluation script that supports multiple baseline methods. The baselines serve as comparison points for learned generative models by using simple heuristics based on spatial proximity or random selection.
   292	
   293	The following baseline methods are supported:
   294	- RdnAcross: Randomly samples a RIR from the entire dataset. This baseline ignores all spatial information and serves as a lower bound on performance.
   295	- RdnSame: Randomly samples a RIR from the same room/scene as the target. This baseline uses room identity but ignores the specific source-receiver positions.
   296	- KNN: K-Nearest Neighbor approach that selects the reference RIR whose source position is closest to the target source position. This baseline uses explicit spatial reasoning with `--num-shot` reference examples.
   297	- LinearInterp: Linear interpolation of multiple reference RIRs weighted by inverse distance to the target source position. Uses `--num-shot` reference examples and performs weighted interpolation in the waveform domain.
   298	
   299	The `eval_baselines.py` script handles both AR and HAA datasets:
   300	
   301	```bash
   302	# AR (KNN 8-shot unseen evaluation)
   303	python -m baselines.eval_baselines \
   304	--dataset AR \
   305	--baseline KNN \
   306	--num-shot 8 \
   307	--split unseen \
   308	--data-path /path/to/AR/dataset \
   309	--seen-json data/AR/seen_eval.json \
   310	--ckpt-AGREE weights/AGREE/AGREE_fullAR.pt \
   311	--out-dir baselines_results
   312	
   313	# HAA (RdnAcross test evaluation)
   314	python -m baselines.eval_baselines \
   315	--dataset HAA \
   316	--baseline RdnAcross \
   317	--split-file data/HAA/test_base.json \
   318	--data-path /path/to/HAA_dataset \
   319	--ckpt-AGREE weights/AGREE/AGREE_fullHAA.pt \
   320	--out-dir baselines_results/
   321	```
